sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Farhadifar et al. (2007) Drosophila wing disc apical vertex model, Lewis's law packing & PCP (Fz/Stbm) hinge-contraction vertex dynamics faithfully reproduces Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium (vendored specimen micrograph is a Mus musculus epithelium — see transfer_boundary) morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium (vendored specimen micrograph is a Mus musculus epithelium — see transfer_boundary) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 84.8/100, audit 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_wing_vertex_model_comparison.png; organism: Fruit fly (Drosophila melanogaster) 3rd-instar larval wing imaginal disc & pupal wing epithelium (vendored specimen micrograph is a Mus musculus epithelium — see transfer_boundary); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/7e4f207; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 00f70e92aaa338b22956554153bb93fbccd372cdaae2e3f47f4744bcadfffe52; artifact_sha256: 2cb99062ead6793102bd757b45c1c91c5b484d3f97e6a67b428f78f2fbb36aa7; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Farhadifar, Röper, Aigouy, Eaton & Jülicher (2007) Current Biology Eqs. 1-2 & Fig. 2A: apical epithelial vertex energy functional E({r_i}) = sum (K/2)(A_alpha - A^(0))^2 + sum Lambda_{ij} l_{ij} + sum (Gamma/2) L_alpha^2 parameterized by (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar), partitioning ground states into Case I (rigid hexagonal, canonical wing disc Lambda_bar=0.12, Gamma_bar=0.04), Case II (soft network), and Case III (cell collapse). | Farhadifar et al. (2007) Fig. 3-4, Gibson et al. (2006) Nature & Classen et al. (2005) Dev. Cell: proliferating 3rd-instar Drosophila wing disc exhibits P(6) approx 0.455 and obeys Lewis's Law <A_n>/<A> = (n-2)/4, whereas post-mitotic pupal wing annealing increases P(6) to ~0.78, and PCP (fz, stbm) mutants fail to reach wild-type hexagonal order. | Aigouy et al. (2010) Cell & Etournay et al. (2015) eLife: hinge contraction from ~15 hAPF stretches the blade along the proximal-distal axis, cells elongate along PD and then relax through oriented cell rearrangements while the Fz/Stbm PCP axis reorients to PD; tissue shear decomposes into cell-elongation change plus rearrangement, division and correlation contributions.; reconstructed_in_script: 2D periodic Voronoi-seed (Lloyd-type) packing and mitotic cleavage simulation across 4 regimes (Proliferating Wing Disc, Post-Mitotic Pupal Wing, High-Contractility Case I, Soft Case II), 2D (Lambda_bar, Gamma_bar) phase diagram, UV laser junction ablation recoil curves, and 7-point continuous Lambda_bar sweep (Section 2, panels A1-A4, B1-B5). | Pass 3: explicit tri-cellular vertex model (analytic forces of Eq. 1, T1 exchanges) on a 100-cell patch with a per-bond Frizzled/Strabismus asymmetry tensor Q_ab modulating line tension Lambda_ab = Lambda_bar (1 + eps_pcp n.Q_ab.n), Fz-Stbm feedback + flow-alignment polarity dynamics, an area-preserving hinge-contraction boundary strain diag(lambda, 1/lambda) with ln lambda = 0.35, shear decomposition into cell-elongation and rearrangement parts, a PCP loss-of-function (eps_pcp = 0) control and a 6-point eps_pcp sweep (Section 2b, panels C1-C5, GIF panel 4). | Junction-guided Voronoi-watershed segmentation of the vendored apical junction-stained polygonal epithelial micrograph (N=37 interior cells, P(6)=0.4865, P(n) correlation r = 0.9913 against the Farhadifar wing-disc distribution).; transfer_boundary: 2D apical junctional projection of 3D pseudostratified/columnar wing imaginal disc epithelial cells. | The vendored specimen `drosophila_wing_epithelium_specimen.jpg` is a Wikimedia Commons epithelial monolayer whose scout manifest records organism Mus musculus; its polygon statistics are compared with Drosophila literature values as a cross-species epithelial-packing transfer, not as a Drosophila specimen. | The Section 2 regimes are Voronoi-seed relaxations with a post-hoc Lewis's-law area reweighting and a hexagonal-lattice pull in the pupal regime; only Section 2b integrates the Farhadifar energy on vertex degrees of freedom. | The PCP coupling sign (PCP-complex-bearing AP junctions stiffened for eps_pcp > 0), the polarity-dynamics gains (k_fb = 0.6, k_flow = 0.4), the initial polarity spread (0.6 rad) and the hinge log-strain (0.35) are modelling choices, not fitted to data; Pass 3 reference values from Etournay (2015) and Classen (2005) are approximate figure reads recorded offline.; does_not_claim: Does not model basal extracellular matrix curvature, 3D apico-basal scutoid transitions, Fat/Dachsous polarity, the pre-15 hAPF margin-directed PCP pattern, cell divisions or extrusions during pupal morphogenesis, the hinge as a separate mechanical compartment, or periodic boundary conditions for the explicit vertex model (the patch is clamped at its margin). | Does not claim to reproduce the Classen et al. (2005) PCP-mutant loss of hexagonal order: in this model the PCP coupling lowers the final hexagon fraction (sign mismatch disclosed in measurement `pcp_wt_minus_mutant_hexagonal_fraction_delta`).]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1002/ar.1090380305>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2010.07.042>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2007.11.049>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2005.10.016>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature05014>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1080/13642810108205772>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.094060>,
            <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.07090> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.848"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/7e4f207/2007-farhadifar-drosophila-wing-vertex-model.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
